      "receiptId": "green-goose-pie.html-1",
      "receiptSource": "Original Receipt in \u0027\u003Ci\u003EThe Closet Of Sir Kenelm Digby Knight, Opened\u003C/i\u003E \u0027 (\u003Ca href=\u0022references.html#digby-1669\u0022\u003E\u003Cb\u003EDigby 1669\u003C/b\u003E\u003C/a\u003E)",
      "receiptText": "\u003Cb\u003EGREEN-GEESE-PYE\u003C/b\u003E\u003Cbr\u003E\nAn excellent cold Pye is thus made. Take two fat Green-geese; bone them, and lay them in paste one upon the other, seasoning them well with Pepper and Salt, and some little Nutmeg, both above and below and between the two Geese. When it is well-baked and out of the oven, pour in melted butter at a hole made in the top. The crust is much better than of a Stubble-goose.\u003Cbr\u003E"
    }
